      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Marcus Ashford.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. XP ledger: level 3, power rating 6 → a level 3 Rogue player-character sheet (a player may take this seat; the authored CR 3 stands in where the ledger is silent). Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>Onyx Hand Representative</strong> — Onyx Hand</p><p>Status: Active — Operating within the Shadow Estate during succession crisis</p><p>Marcus Ashford is an Onyx Hand representative who appeared during the confrontation between guards and Disaster Inc., de-escalating a near-battle by offering Remi a 'nearly empty supply kit' that turned her eyes blue and caused black smoke to emerge from a wound. He also pickpocketed a pink paper from Bowser—observed by the toads but not mentioned at the time. Marcus speaks in rhyming verse, taunts enemies with theatrical flair, and represents organized Iron Legion/Onyx Hand interests within the Shadow Estate. Whether he's helping, manipulating, or both remains unclear.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Concealed Blade</strong> — “Onyx Hand Representative”</li><li><strong>De-escalation</strong> — “Marcus Ashford is an Onyx Hand representative who appeared during the confrontation between guards and Disaster Inc., de-escalating a near-battle by offering Remi a 'nearly empty supply kit' that turned her eyes blue”</li><li><strong>Nearly Empty Supply Kit</strong> — “Marcus Ashford is an Onyx Hand representative who appeared during the confrontation between guards and Disaster Inc., de-escalating a near-battle by offering Remi a 'nearly empty supply kit' that turned her eyes blue”</li><li><strong>Own Agenda</strong> — “Waluigi is documenting Marcus Ashford based on his appearance during the escalating confrontation at the Shadow Estate—a confrontation he DE-escalated while simultaneously pursuing his own agenda.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/marcus_ashford</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/marcus_ashford</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
